From: Alberto Cavalcante <alberto@cavalcante.uk>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:21:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] docs: attribute fork modifications to Alberto Cavalcante (#1)

Identify Alberto Cavalcante's fork modifications separately from upstream
Starlark code. Preserve the upstream license and copyright notices.

Validated with canonical Go 1.22.12 checks, the hosted three-OS/four-Go
matrix, and independent review of all attribution changes.

Squashed from:
- 4a8854061a0cfd64b375db32f1854ad02d8b2b24
---
 FORK_NOTICE           | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 starlark/eval.go      |  1 +
 starlark/eval_test.go |  1 +
 starlark/interp.go    |  4 ++++
 starlark/value.go     |  1 +
 syntax/options.go     |  1 +
 syntax/parse.go       |  1 +
 syntax/parse_test.go  |  1 +
 syntax/scan.go        |  1 +
 syntax/scan_test.go   |  1 +
 syntax/syntax.go      |  1 +
 syntax/walk.go        |  1 +
 12 files changed, 32 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 FORK_NOTICE

diff --git a/FORK_NOTICE b/FORK_NOTICE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..eb1f70fc753f245e3fd4f0c92fd2dd5912dff749
--- /dev/null
+++ b/FORK_NOTICE
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+starlark-go-x copyright attribution
+
+Upstream starlark-go retains its original copyright notices and BSD-style
+license in LICENSE. Those notices apply to the upstream work.
+
+Fork-specific additions and modifications authored by Alberto Cavalcante
+are Copyright (c) 2026 Alberto Cavalcante. All rights reserved. These include
+the execution, branch, function and iteration hooks, source-position API,
+and type-annotation parsing extensions introduced after upstream commit
+3fee463870c9e2f24e391952f5cf5e95463357b4, and their associated tests.
+
+Files containing both upstream work and fork modifications retain upstream
+notices and identify Alberto Cavalcante's modifications separately. New
+files authored for this fork carry Alberto Cavalcante's copyright notice.
+
+The fork modifications use the BSD-style license in LICENSE. This notice
+identifies their copyright holder; it does not assign their copyright to
+the upstream project or The Bazel Authors.
